<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for 377bln lire of Italy 30-yr Btp.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for 377bln lire of Italy 30-yr Btp.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for 377 billion lire of 30-year fixed-rate bonds (BTP) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 150 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 2.337 trillion lire at the open auction for the November 1, 2026 paper, against 1.5 trillion lire worth of bonds on offer and the auction price was set at 100.55.</p>
</text>
